{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"rubidium-magnific-billygoat","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nTwenty ADRs describe one subsystem (titles confirmed by `git ls-tree origin/main -- docs/adr`): 0004 snapshot contract, 0026 three-way-merge baseline, 0027 binding lifecycle, 0028 bound-but-absent, 0029 status/echo, 0031 ref-lock, 0055 Jira-family sub-seam, 0060 bridge-state formats, 0062 pagination stall, 0083 vendor-adapter seam, 0084 ACLI 429 backoff, 0085 live-validation harness, 0092 bridge vocabulary, 0094 last-pass two-witness, 0095 DC wiki renderer, 0096 Pandoc corpus, 0097 many-to-many projects, 0099 binding-store ownership, 0103 operation coordination, 0107 typed mutation payload. Overrides among them: 0055 AMENDS 0083 (`0055…md:5,9`); 0092's adapters paragraph is overridden by its S2 amendment; 0031's C2/C3/C4 sections and 0107 §4/§Open items are landed transitions (epics `6c9c-811f-6dc4-40e7`, story `e9d5-c850-d505-4a5a` closed); 0027's amendment fixes the `rebar bridge fsck` spelling. Everything else is additive (0103 retains 0084 jitter `:44-46`; 0107 §5 leaves 0004/0026/0027/0028/0029/0083/0092 unaffected).\n\n## Approach\nWrite `docs/adr/0119-reconciler-architecture-consolidated-record.md` — **final-form decision statements, not verbatim copies** (target 400–600 lines; originals remain the verbatim evidence). Header: `**Status:** Accepted — consolidates ADRs 0004, 0026, 0027, 0028, 0029, 0031, 0055, 0060, 0062, 0083, 0084, 0085, 0092, 0094, 0095, 0096, 0097, 0099, 0103, 0107.` Rule stated up front: one section per surviving decision, the originating ADR in the heading; where a later ADR overrode an earlier one the decision appears once in final form with a \"supersedes ADR 00xx §y\" note. Section outline (headings verbatim, `### N. Title — from ADR 00xx`):\n\n- Part A Data contracts: 1. Producer↔consumer snapshot contract and the rules for new reconciler tests — 0004; 2. Typed mutation payload, a discriminated union by (direction, action), and its ownership table — 0107 (§4 sequencing and §Open items recorded as landed history); 3. Bridge state stays committed, formats cheap (A1, A2, A3, A4-2) — 0060; 4. The project set belongs to the store; legacy migration writes no ticket events; capability stamped conditionally — 0097.\n- Part B Arbitration: 5. Three-way-merge baseline and direction arbitration — 0026; 6. Canonical reverse status map, provenance+single-pass echo suppression, exact-match assignee — 0029; 7. Bound-but-absent ≠ deleted: deletion proven only by bounded direct GET 404 — 0028.\n- Part C Bindings: 8. Binding lifecycle pending→confirmed→retired, adoption gating, audit vocabulary `rebar bridge fsck` — 0027 (+amendment); 9. Binding-store internal ownership behind one facade (open views, shallow `all_bindings()`, three failure dispositions, ordered partial states, repair-before-first-observation, explicit `unretire`, persistence ≠ publication) — 0099.\n- Part D Coordination: 10. Bare-ref CAS pass-lock/phase-gate, lease self-healing, ref backend only — 0031 (supersedes 0031 §\"Band-aid retirement\" transitional text; break-glass commands → runbook pointer, see S4); 11. Last-pass two-witness status — 0094; 12. Single retry budget + observe-before-replay, eleven-disposition taxonomy, fuse — 0103 (§\"S1 lifecycle boundary\" recorded as landed); 13. ACLI subprocess 429 backoff, retained beneath 0103 — 0084; 14. A stalled pager aborts past fail-open handlers — 0062.\n- Part E Vendor seam and Jira family: 15. Jira-neutral core + `adapters/<backend>/`, Phase 2 landed, proof-of-seam claim as narrowed — 0083 (supersedes 0083 §(g)/proof-of-seam per 0055); 16. Jira-family sub-seam, shared `jira` provenance, DC horizon 2029-03-28 — 0055; 17. DC Markdown→wiki segmenting, verify-then-fall-back renderer, pins 3.9/1.17 — 0095; 18. Complete Pandoc corpus replay in external integration — 0096.\n- Part F Operator surface: 19. Bridge-primary vocabulary; adapters removed, `--filter-local-ids` engine-only survives — 0092 (supersedes 0092 §Decision ¶2); 20. Live-validation harness: deterministic core + live probes under bilateral teardown — 0085 (§4 report → runbook pointer, S4).\n- Appendix A Rejected alternatives (collected from 0055 (i), 0060, 0062, 0094, 0095, 0096, 0099 §9). Appendix B Provenance table ADR → section(s).\n\nThen in each of the 20 originals change the status to `**Status:** Archived — consolidated into [ADR 0119](0119-reconciler-architecture-consolidated-record.md)` (keep the original status text in parentheses after it, e.g. `(was: Accepted (epic adept-hedge-stain / d01e))`) and add the banner `> **Archived (2026-09-07).** Consolidated into [ADR 0119](…) §N; kept verbatim as the evidence record.` Bodies untouched (tests pin them: `test_wiki_render.py:329-347` needs 0095's six headings + \"3.9\"/\"1.17\"; `test_apply_handlers_operation_outcome.py:367-378` needs \"s3\", \"cutover\", \"fuse\", \"retire\" in 0103). Run `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py` (adds `docs/adr/.numbers/0119` and the index row under \"Reconciler & Jira sync\"). Do not write \"success criteria\"/\"SC\" in 0119 (`scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py`, no ADR is allowlisted) and no bot e-mail (`check_dco_identity.py`).\n\n## Scope\nNew: `docs/adr/0119-reconciler-architecture-consolidated-record.md`, `docs/adr/.numbers/0119` (generated). Edit: the 20 originals' status line + banner, `docs/adr/README.md` (generated). Not: 0070 (config CLI), 0087 (LLM transport), 0111.\n\n## Testing\n`python scripts/check_adr_numbers.py`; `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check`; `python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check`; `python scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py`; `python scripts/check_dco_identity.py`; `pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_adr_0095_records_the_required_sections tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_apply_handlers_operation_outcome.py::test_adr_0103_names_s3_as_cutover_owner tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py tests/scripts/test_check_adr_numbers.py tests/unit/test_gerrit_docs_only.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0119-…md` exists with 20 `### N. … — from ADR 00xx` headings covering exactly the 20 numbers (verify: `grep -oE 'from ADR 0[0-9]{3}' | sort -u | wc -l` = 20) and at least three \"supersedes ADR 00xx\" notes (0031, 0083, 0092).\n- [ ] Each of the 20 originals contains `Archived — consolidated into [ADR 0119]` on its status line (`grep -l | wc -l` = 20) and its pre-existing `## ` headings are unchanged (`git diff -U0 -- docs/adr/00xx-*.md | grep '^[-+]#'` empty).\n- [ ] `docs/adr/.numbers/0119` content is `0119-reconciler-architecture-consolidated-record.md`; both ADR gates exit 0.","id":"8257-3a28-e757-4079","parent_id":"cdac-532f-0edb-422d","priority":3,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Write ADR 0119, the consolidated reconciler architecture record, and archive the twenty originals"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788808060417836476,"uuid":"f7d92222-82ce-42a3-833a-7dda46c2ce97"}